From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 19:37:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] local_backend: allow startup isolate memory overcommit

Add a strict startup planning percentage for aggregate isolate heap and ArrayBuffer ceilings. Keep the default at 100 percent so existing deployments retain conservative feasibility checks, while self-hosted operators can select a measured aggregate commitment below the sum of independent per-worker limits.\n\nApply the percentage only to isolate memory accounting. Cache budgets, the complete local Node allowance, the native and kernel reserve, runtime isolate limits, and the finite cgroup boundary remain unchanged.\n\nPublish the selected percentage together with raw and accounted isolate capacity, pass the knob through the maintained Compose file, and document the operational contract.
